I was once again attempting to start up an interesting game and ran into
a peculiarly situated chest.  As a matter of course, I try to loot chests
whenever possible, but when I tried to move onto this chest, I ended up
falling through a trap door!  Which leads me to wonder: would it make more
sense if the chest fell through the trap door too and was perhaps smashed
at the bottom of its fall?

Here's my question from before which was never answered but still is a
curiosity for me.  What exactly does the dexterity statistic cover?  This
really became a question for me when I unwittingly discovered 'gloves of
fumbling' and I started tripping all over.  My dexterity stat never changed
though.  It's probably not a bug, I realize, since I've worn cursed boots
before with the same effect - a loss of dexterity (or newly found clumsiness)
with no decrease in the dexterity statistic.

